{"agent_id":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:42:24.885134550Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7ef840e7-d516-4301-b94d-f02d6d30bb55","comment_uuid":"28507c0a-1946-45a8-97ed-54c47674ce8f","author":"pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a","content":"Plan: Decision-ready comparison of 3 candidate approaches for the C2 (consistently-drifted backend) gap.\n\nEnvironment confirmed: toolregistry==0.15.0, mcp==2.0.0, py3.10.12 venv at /tmp/toolregistry-venv (reused, not reinstalled). Source-read the installed package: the C2 RuntimeError is raised by the mcp SDK itself (mcp/client/session.py:1110 validate_tool_result, called from ClientSession.call_tool:1064); ToolRegistry does NOT raise it — MCPClient.call_tool (client.py:133) is a pass-through, and MCPConnectionManager._call_persistent (connection.py:103-111) catches ANY exception and reconnects. No public hook/factory/callback in integration.py/connection.py/client.py; register_from_mcp hardcodes MCPConnectionManager construction. Two candidate seams for B: subclass MCPConnectionManager (public class) or MCPClient (public class) + manual registration assembly via public MCPTool.from_tool_json / registry.register.\n\nApproach:\nA. Build proxy_self_heal.py in a clean dir research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/ (byte-identical copies of backend.py/manifest.json, md5-verified; copy of drift proxy.py + documented self-heal deltas): per-tool failure counter; on N consecutive schema-validation failures vs the proxy's OWN served manifest (N=1 strictest first), capture live response shape and update served manifest; persist heal state so a reconnect-respawned proxy serves the corrected manifest; log every heal event. Tests: C2 scenario (repeated calls; record first-call cost, post-heal cost vs normal-success baseline, heal count to stabilize), other-tools-untouched (multiply), intermittent-drift flapping check (N=1 then a higher N to find the flapping threshold).\nB. Reproduce C2 with FULL tracebacks (monkeypatch _call_persistent in the test harness only to capture traceback.format_exc() at the reconnect trigger, then re-raise). Identify SDK-vs-ToolRegistry origin from traceback + source. Build the SMALLEST PoC wrapper (subclass MCPConnectionManager overriding the persistent-call path to classify schema-validation RuntimeError as terminal: no reconnect) + manual registration assembly, test against C2, record code size and whether it closes the gap. If no clean point: STOP and record (no fragile patch).\nC. Only if B finds no clean point — minimal connection.py diff estimate + upgrade-fragility assessment, PoC-tested once.\n\nDeliverable: report.md (Documentation Standard YAML: program EDASES, layer Research, document_type Research Finding) with A's before/after numbers + flapping result, B's YES/NO + traceback + PoC size, C only if reached, one-paragraph recommendation; plus logs/ and PoC scripts. Observation/finding separation; exact versions; verbatim error text. No modification of #213/#217 corpora; stdio only; PoC quality only.","created_at":"2026-08-06T07:42:24.879310088Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA4bvhvfJIdqty05aHuXaO12/nb4pwW/1pSp4aSaoWDHYXMuyZdiv5bsynSwS494/qVTC9daDZmeckRwm1WIeXAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:QnesEmvvqpIlj5hRSf8Xgt2fnafYnIlPGS2VybcvWMc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg3GZ1ioft4osqukNxK8O3e9w3xIKe6PwYDD2kPknQ0QMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBnmiVOjK6dj/CSFOk5ZBNbA3HEt4946D4XSRNaMN2yve5lWID9v6xYLgIvrB85ncaZ1oSLfSshrcc3sLEvfQQU="}
